quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  2,170,"Moreover, when they are told: ‘Follow what Allah has revealed,’ they say: ‘We will instead follow what we have found our fathers practising.’ Even though their fathers neither applied any reason (to understand the truth) nor were they guided."
  2,171,"And the parable of (inviting) the disbelievers (to guidance) is that of someone who calls on that which can hear nothing but a shout and a cry. Deaf, dumb and blind, they understand nothing."
  2,172,"O believers! Eat of the good things We have provided you, and be grateful to Allah if it is He Whom you worship."
  2,173,"He has only forbidden you carrion, blood, the flesh of swine and animals over which any name other than Allah’s has been invoked while slaughtering. But whoever is compelled by extreme necessity (to eat any of these), neither intending to disobey nor transgress, there shall be no sin upon him. Allah is indeed Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  2,174,"Indeed, those who conceal any part of the Book Allah has revealed and sell it for a paltry gain shall swallow nothing but fire into their bellies. Allah shall neither speak to them on the Day of Resurrection nor purify them. And there is a painful punishment for them."
  2,175,They are the ones who bought error for guidance and punishment for pardon. What has made them patient to face the Fire?
  2,176,This is because Allah has revealed the Book with the truth. So those who differ about the Book are surely in extreme defiance.
